// zm_qol - display names for the three ported T5 wonder weapons.
// Without these the HUD prints the raw localize key, e.g.
// "ZOMBIE_WEAPON_FREEZEGUN_UPGRADED", which is what the user reported.
// BO2 ships NO localize entry for any of these six keys - verified by grepping
// the localize assets of all 191 fastfiles in zone\all.
VERSION             "1"
CONFIG              "C:/projects/cod/t6/bin/StringEd.cfg"
FILENOTES           ""

REFERENCE           ZOMBIE_WEAPON_THUNDERGUN
LANG_ENGLISH        "Thundergun"

REFERENCE           ZOMBIE_WEAPON_THUNDERGUN_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "Zeus Cannon"

REFERENCE           ZOMBIE_WEAPON_TESLA
LANG_ENGLISH        "Wunderwaffe DG-2"

REFERENCE           ZOMBIE_WEAPON_TESLA_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "Wunderwaffe DG-3 JZ"

REFERENCE           ZOMBIE_WEAPON_FREEZEGUN
LANG_ENGLISH        "Winter's Howl"

REFERENCE           ZOMBIE_WEAPON_FREEZEGUN_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "Winter's Fury"

// ============================================================================
//  v1.89.0 - THE 9 PORTED MULTIPLAYER WEAPONS.
//
//  Only 11 of the 22 display refs these weapons use need shipping. The other
//  11 already resolve on a zombies map - VERIFIED by dumping the localize asset
//  of every en_*.ff a zombies map loads (en_code_post_gfx_zm, en_common_zm,
//  en_patch_zm, en_ui_zm, en_<map>, the dlc loads and the so_z* transit set)
//  and matching each REFERENCE. "SWAT-556", "FAL OSW", "Mk 48", "QBB LSW",
//  "MP7", "Vector K10", "MSMC", "Crossbow", "Grenade Launcher", "Semtex" and
//  "Awful Lawton" are all already there, so re-declaring them would put a
//  second definition in front of the map that owns it for no gain.
//
//  🛑 THE TEXT IS NOT INVENTED. The base names are Treyarch's own, read out of
//  the MP language fastfiles; the Pack-a-Punch names are BO2-Reimagined's, read
//  out of english\localizedstrings\reimagined.str. Nothing here was typed from
//  memory.
//
//  📝 WEAPON_PEACEKEEPER is the one BASE name that must ship: the Peacekeeper is
//  a DLC weapon and its string lives in the MP patch language zone only, which
//  no zombies map loads.
// ============================================================================

REFERENCE           WEAPON_PEACEKEEPER
LANG_ENGLISH        "Peacekeeper"

REFERENCE           ZMWEAPON_SIG556_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "FBI-667"

REFERENCE           ZMWEAPON_SA58_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "WN OTW"

REFERENCE           ZMWEAPON_MK48_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "HtMk 4800"

REFERENCE           ZMWEAPON_QBB95_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "RCC MTX"

REFERENCE           ZMWEAPON_MP7_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "Matter Penetrator 700"

REFERENCE           ZMWEAPON_VECTOR_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "Matrix K1000"

REFERENCE           ZMWEAPON_VECTOR_EXTCLIP
LANG_ENGLISH        "Vector K10 Extended Clip"

REFERENCE           ZMWEAPON_VECTOR_EXTCLIP_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "Matrix K1000 Extended Clip"

REFERENCE           ZMWEAPON_INSAS_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "Modern Sub Machine Catastrophe"

REFERENCE           ZMWEAPON_PEACEKEEPER_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "Warmonger"

// ============================================================================
//  v1.92.0 - THE XPR-50 (asset name `as50`), weapon 10.
//
//  Only the Pack-a-Punch name ships. The BASE name WEAPON_AS50 ("XPR-50")
//  already resolves on a zombies map - it is present in BOTH en_patch_zm.ff and
//  en_code_post_gfx_zm.ff, confirmed by dumping the localize asset of each with
//  the Unlinker and matching the REFERENCE. Re-declaring it would put a second
//  definition in front of the fastfile that owns it for no gain.
//
//  🛑 The text below is BO2-Reimagined's, read out of
//  english\localizedstrings\reimagined.str - not typed from memory, same rule
//  as the eleven above.
// ============================================================================

REFERENCE           ZMWEAPON_AS50_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "Xtreme Pain Releaser 5000"

// ============================================================================
//  v1.93.0 - THE TITUS-6, weapon 11 and the last of the port.
//
//  Only the Pack-a-Punch name ships. Both BASE names already resolve on a
//  zombies map - WEAPON_TITUS6_EXPLOSIVE ("Titus-6") and WEAPON_TITUS6
//  ("Buckshot", the masterkey mode) are each present in the zombies language
//  fastfiles, confirmed by dumping the localize asset of en_code_post_gfx_zm,
//  en_common_zm, en_patch_zm, en_ui_zm and two map zones and matching the
//  REFERENCE. Text below is BO2-Reimagined's, out of reimagined.str.
// ============================================================================

REFERENCE           ZMWEAPON_TITUS6_EXPLOSIVE_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "Augustus-9"

// ============================================================================
//  v1.99.13 - THE TAC-45 (asset name `fnp45`), weapon 12.
//
//  Only the Pack-a-Punch name ships. The BASE name WEAPON_FNP45 already resolves
//  on a zombies map - it is present in en_code_post_gfx_zm.ff (and in
//  en_code_post_gfx_mp.ff and en_patch.ff), found by grepping an index of all
//  191 fastfiles for `localize, WEAPON_FNP45`. Re-declaring it would put a
//  second definition in front of the fastfile that owns it for no gain - the
//  same call made for the XPR-50 and the Titus-6.
//
//  🛑 ZMWEAPON_FNP45_UPGRADED is in NO fastfile, so it has to be ours. Text
//  below is BO2-Reimagined's, read out of english\localizedstrings\reimagined.str
//  line 1214 - not invented, same rule as the eleven above. It is a dual-wield
//  pair when packed, which is what the name is playing on.
// ============================================================================

REFERENCE           ZMWEAPON_FNP45_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "Toughguy & Crybaby"

// ============================================================================
//  v2.9.9 - THE CAMPAIGN DRAGUNOV, weapon 13 of the port (user task 1,
//  2026-08-30).
//
//  BOTH names have to be ours. WEAPON_DRAGUNOV exists only in the CAMPAIGN
//  language fastfiles - the zombies pair (en_patch_zm / en_code_post_gfx_zm,
//  both dumped and grepped) carries only ZOMBIE_WEAPON_DRAGUNOV, a cut wall-buy
//  hint. The Pack-a-Punch name is NOT invented: "D115 Disassembler" is BO1's
//  own name for this exact gun's upgrade, read out of BO1's
//  en_common_zombie.ff string table (key ZOMBIE_DRAGUNOV_UPGRADED) - the same
//  read-the-real-thing rule as every name above.
// ============================================================================

REFERENCE           WEAPON_DRAGUNOV
LANG_ENGLISH        "Dragunov"

REFERENCE           ZMWEAPON_DRAGUNOV_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "D115 Disassembler"

// v2.9.9 - the Bouncing Betty (user task 4). The MP key BOUNCING_BETTY lives
// only in the MP language fastfiles, so the def and the box hint both use this
// mod-owned key instead.

REFERENCE           ZMWEAPON_BOUNCINGBETTY
LANG_ENGLISH        "Bouncing Betty"

// v2.9.13 - the EMP grenade, now a box weapon on every map (user request).
// Stock zm_transit.gsc:2017 passes &"ZOMBIE_WEAPON_EMP_GRENADE" to
// add_zombie_weapon(), but that key is in NO localize asset this project could
// find - not zm_transit.ff (0 localize assets), not en_zm_transit.ff (9, none
// of them this), not en_common_zm / en_patch_zm / en_ui_zm. Without an entry
// the box prints the raw key, which is what happened to the three wonder
// weapons above. The text matches what TranZit shows today, so that map is
// unchanged and the other five simply gain the same name.

REFERENCE           ZOMBIE_WEAPON_EMP_GRENADE
LANG_ENGLISH        "EMP Grenade"


// ============================================================================
//  v2.10.14 - THE WAVE GUN, complete (was: v2.9.18 the Zap Guns alone).
//  The keys are Treyarch's own, read out of the six microwavegun* defs
//  (displayName\ZOMBIE_WEAPON_MICROWAVEGUN[DW][_UPGRADED]); the texts are the
//  ones Zombies Declassified's mod_load.ff localizes them to - i.e. Treyarch's
//  DLC5 strings, measured 2026-09-03 with Unlinker --include-assets localize.

REFERENCE           ZOMBIE_WEAPON_MICROWAVEGUNDW
LANG_ENGLISH        "Zap Gun Dual Wield"

REFERENCE           ZOMBIE_WEAPON_MICROWAVEGUNDW_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "Porter's X2 Zap Gun Dual Wield"

REFERENCE           ZOMBIE_WEAPON_MICROWAVEGUN
LANG_ENGLISH        "Wave Gun"

REFERENCE           ZOMBIE_WEAPON_MICROWAVEGUN_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "Max Wave Gun"


// ============================================================================
//  v2.9.18 - THE CAMPAIGN SPAS-12. Both keys are Treyarch's own, read out of
//  the defs: WEAPON_SPAS is the campaign def's displayName (its string lives
//  only in SP language zones no zombies map loads), and ZOMBIE_SPAS_UPGRADED
//  is BO1's key from raw\weapons\sp\spas_upgraded_zm. The Pack-a-Punch name
//  is BO1's official one - the SPAZ-24 - which its 24-round clip in that same
//  def corroborates. The user's message wrote "SPA-Z"; "SPAZ-24" is what BO1
//  actually called it, and "official BO1 name" was the instruction.
// ============================================================================

REFERENCE           WEAPON_SPAS
LANG_ENGLISH        "SPAS-12"

REFERENCE           ZOMBIE_SPAS_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "SPAZ-24"

// ============================================================================
//  v2.12.7 - THE THREE ZOMBIES CONTROL-BIND LABELS (user, 2026-09-06).
//
//  These three rows in the CONTROLS list are multiplayer leftovers: Zombies has
//  no scorestreaks, so the stock text described nothing the buttons do. Renamed
//  to what the bound action slot actually is.
//
//  🛑 THESE ARE STOCK KEYS THIS MOD IS NOW OVERRIDING - the first time this file
//  has done that on purpose, so the mechanism was measured rather than assumed:
//    * localize is a PER-KEY asset type in T6, not one blob. `Unlinker --list
//      mod.ff` prints 30 `localize, <KEY>` rows, exactly the 30 REFERENCEs in
//      this file, so `localize,mod` in mod_wonderweapons.zone already turns each
//      entry below into its own asset. No .zone edit is needed to add one.
//    * All three keys are owned by en_code_post_gfx_zm.ff (every zombies map
//      loads it) and again by en_patch.ff - dumped both with
//      `Unlinker --include-assets localize` and matched the REFERENCE.
//    * A mod fastfile's copy WINS. The precedent is BO2-Reimagined, which
//      overrides 14 keys that en_code_post_gfx_zm also owns, with different
//      text - including PLATFORM_PICKUPNEWWEAPON and GAME_BUTTON_TO_REVIVE_PLAYER
//      (the same PLATFORM_* prompt class as these) and MENU_RESTART_LEVEL_CAPS
//      -> "RESTART GAME", which is this exact kind of menu-label change.
//
//  📝 The label-to-slot pairing is the USER'S OWN READING of their controls
//  screen and could NOT be settled offline - BO2's keybind table is code-side,
//  not in any fastfile. Corroboration, not proof: BO1's controls menu
//  (raw/ui/options_shoot_pc.menu:117) binds "@PLATFORM_USE_EQUIPMENT_CAPS" to
//  "+actionslot 1", and slot 1 is where this mod puts the Jet Gun
//  (zm_transit.gsc) - so slot 1 = equipment holds in both games.
//  🛑 IF THE RENAMED ROWS TURN OUT TO SIT ON THE WRONG BINDS, the other
//  candidate set is BO2's own PLATFORM_GROUND_SUPPORT_CAPS / _AIR_SUPPORT_ /
//  _USE_GEAR_ / _USE_EQUIPMENT_CAPS, which read "SPECIAL ACTION 1".."4".
// ============================================================================

REFERENCE           PLATFORM_NEXT_SCORE_STREAK_CAPS
LANG_ENGLISH        "EQUIPMENT"

REFERENCE           PLATFORM_PREVIOUS_SCORE_STREAK_CAPS
LANG_ENGLISH        "MELEE WEAPON"

REFERENCE           PLATFORM_ACTIVATE_SCORE_STREAK_CAPS
LANG_ENGLISH        "PLACEABLE MINE"

// ============================================================================
//  v2.12.7 - THE STORM PSR (internal name metalstorm_mms).
//
//  Only the PACK-A-PUNCH name is shipped here. The base name is NOT ours and
//  must not be redeclared: localize WEAPON_METALSTORM already resolves from
//  en_code_post_gfx_zm.ff, which the game loads on every zombies map -
//  verified 2026-09-06 with Unlinker --list (WEAPON_METALSTORM,
//  WEAPON_METALSTORM_DESC, WEAPON_METALSTORM_DESC_MP are all there). Same
//  situation as WEAPON_AS50, noted in quality_of_life.gsc.
//
//  "Tempest PTR" is BO2-Reimagined's own upgraded name for this gun, read
//  from english\localizedstrings\reimagined.str:1255. The Storm PSR was
//  never a stock zombies weapon, so no official Treyarch Pack-a-Punch name
//  exists to use instead - unlike the Dragunov, whose "D115 Disassembler"
//  came out of BO1's own string table.
// ============================================================================

REFERENCE           ZMWEAPON_METALSTORM_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "Tempest PTR"

// ============================================================================
//  v2.15.0 - THE FOUR BLACK OPS 1 GUNS (user request 2026-09-09).
//
//  Only four keys are here because the other four already resolve on every
//  zombies map and shipping them would be a pointless override - dumped from
//  the retail english zones to check, not assumed:
//      WEAPON_M60         "M60"        en_code_post_gfx_zm.ff
//      WEAPON_BROWNINGHP  "Browning HP"  en_code_post_gfx_zm.ff
//      WEAPON_RPG         "RPG-7"      en_code_post_gfx_zm.ff
//      ZMWEAPON_USRPG_UPGRADED  "Rocket Propelled Grievance"  en_patch_zm.ff
//  The last one is Treyarch's own Pack-a-Punch name for an RPG in zombies and
//  is what rpg_upgraded_zm already asks for, so the RPG-7 ships no string at all.
//
//  "The Pig" and "L115 Isolator" are BLACK OPS 1's real Pack-a-Punch names for
//  these two guns - the same class of source as the Dragunov's "D115
//  Disassembler". "Bap" is zm_refreshed's own name for the packed Browning HP;
//  the Browning Hi-Power was never a BO1 zombies weapon, so no Treyarch name
//  exists for it - the same situation as the Storm PSR's "Tempest PTR" above.
// ============================================================================

REFERENCE           WEAPON_T5_L96A1
LANG_ENGLISH        "L96A1"

REFERENCE           WEAPON_T5_L96A1_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "L115 Isolator"

REFERENCE           WEAPON_M60_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "The Pig"

REFERENCE           WEAPON_BROWNINGHP_UPGRADED
LANG_ENGLISH        "Bap"

ENDMARKER
